	(text "- Although powered by 12V, the output (Q) voltage was measured to be\n~10.3V. This voltage measurement is important to know since it is the \ngate-to-source voltage for the downstream IRF520 MOSFET driver board \nwhich switches on the LED strips."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5fc71c40-c6a6-4778-8752-6db60356939b")
	)
	(text "NOTES:"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 186.436 56.134 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7b14217e-71b1-4af5-abe2-7d7cbf749abb")
	)
	(text "- The 555 timer is being used in monostable mode. The output\nsignal pulse duration is governed by the 100uF capacitor and \nthe selected resistor value (22k, 33k, or 47k) on the DISCHARGE \nand THRESHOLD pins. The formula is: t = 1.1 * R * C"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.086 59.182 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "998d9033-30ae-4d12-a82b-10da39752df7")
	)
	(text "- The 0.22uF and 10k RC network on the 555's RESET pin form a \nPOR (power-on reset) circuit. During intial power-up testing without\nit, the output (Q) produced occasional HIGH pulses due to undefined \ninternal states of th IC, which turned on downstream LED strips. This RC \nnetwork briefly holds RESET low during power-up, forcing Q in a known \nLOW state while internal circuitry stabilizes. As the 0.22uF capacitor \ncharges, RESET rises to VCC and normal operation begins, preventing \nfalse triggering at startup."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 71.374 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dde1d682-3fb6-45fa-9670-92ffcc07cb38")
	)
